# codev:start
# CoDev bookkeeping paths (ADR-0045) -- marking these generated makes
# GitHub collapse their diff behind a "Load diff" control in the pull
# request view and exclude them from the file list's visual weight,
# instead of adding to a reviewer's load for every bookkeeping commit.
.codev/task/**/*.json linguist-generated=true
.codev/lock.json linguist-generated=true
# codev:end

# Structure fixtures whose SHA-256 is recorded as gold-case provenance, and
# checked against on every verifier run. Git's default text handling would
# rewrite LF to CRLF when checking out on Windows (GitHub's runners set
# core.autocrlf=true), changing the bytes and so the digest -- which is
# exactly what broke //tests/data:generate_real_pymol and
# //tests/data:gold_case_verifier the first time they ran on windows-2025,
# with "structure checksum mismatch" rather than anything to do with the
# targets themselves. Marking them -text pins the working-tree bytes to
# what is committed on every platform, so a recorded digest means the same
# thing everywhere. This applies to the H-02 discovery fixture too, whose
# digest is recorded in docs/codev/wave/evidence/H-02.md.
*.pdb -text
